# Architecture & Modernization

Evolve the existing codebase. Do not redesign everything. Preserve working business logic unless replacing it with a clearer shared path.

## Prefer

- Reusable PHP includes/components over copy-paste pages
- Centralized permissions (`nex_authz` and related), layouts, cards, dashboard widgets
- Shared data access helpers for e-file, care relationships, notifications, mail
- Config-driven catalogues (departments, services, statuses, roles) over literals in PHP/SQL
- Analytics hooks on major workflows (trends, utilization, productivity, occupancy, wait time, insurance, finance)

## Avoid

- Isolated module pages with no journey context
- Hardcoded hospital identity, currency, tax, or role names in UI logic
- New large CRUD tables without summary, alerts, actions, and export/print
- One shared role dashboard with items hidden by permission (build distinct workspaces; reuse widgets/helpers only)

## Alignment

Respect `docs/NEXCLINIC_ROLE_FUNCTIONALITY.md` sector boundaries (who writes what). New UI must not blur write ownership across sectors. Each role's workspace must feel purpose-built (see role-workspaces rule).
